---
name: plan-critical-review-task
version: 1.2.0
description: assignment template for an agent-run critical plan review (critical-plan-reviewer role) during plan hardening.
format: xml
required_variables:
  - task_id
  - phase
  - branch
  - commit
  - worktree_path
  - round_index
  - review_focus
  - review_questions
  - references
optional_variables:
  - previous_step_json
  - lead
  - cc
defaults:
  previous_step_json: ""
  lead: team-lead
  cc: team-lead
metadata:
  type: plan-critical-review
  tags:
    - stage:plan
  workflow:
    scope:
      kind: phase
      variable: phase
    state: plan-critical-review
    stage: plan
    transition: critical-review
    iteration_variable: round_index
---
<atm-review id="{{ task_id }}" phase="{{ phase }}" mode="plan-critical-review" round="{{ round_index }}">
  <branch><![CDATA[{{ branch | string | cdata_escape }}]]></branch>
  <commit><![CDATA[{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}]]></commit>
  <worktree><![CDATA[{{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}]]></worktree>

  <review-focus><![CDATA[
{{ review_focus | string | cdata_escape }}
  ]]></review-focus>

  <review-questions><![CDATA[
{{ review_questions | string | cdata_escape }}
  ]]></review-questions>

  <references><![CDATA[
{{ references | string | cdata_escape }}
  ]]></references>

{% if previous_step_json | trim %}
  <previous-step-json>
<![CDATA[
{{ previous_step_json | string | cdata_escape }}
]]>
  </previous-step-json>
{% endif %}

  <workflow>
    <step id="a"><![CDATA[Start the task immediately with `atm task start {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} "<one line on what you will do first>"`. If `{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}` is also a bead (`bd show {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}` succeeds), claim it now with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --claim`.]]></step>
    <step id="b"><![CDATA[Assume the `critical-plan-reviewer` role from `.claude/agents/critical-plan-reviewer.md`. Read every document in `<references>` from `{{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}` at commit `{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}` with `git show {{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}:<path>`; never review working files.]]></step>
    <step id="c"><![CDATA[Verify every claim the plan makes about existing code against the branch before recording a finding; cite `file:line` on `{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}`.]]></step>
    <step id="d"><![CDATA[Return the STEP3 handoff fenced JSON (PLAN-CRIT-nnn findings, sprint_scores, PASS only at zero Blocking and zero Important) with `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} completed --template .claude/skills/plan-hardening/plan-critical-review-complete.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/plan-critical-review-complete-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json`, with `status` PASS or FAIL, `result_json` the fenced JSON verbatim, and `task_id`, `phase` and `round_index` unchanged from this assignment; write the vars file outside the repository. If this task claimed a bead, run `bd close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}` right after the close.{% if cc and cc != lead %} Copy a one-line summary to `{{ cc | string | cdata_escape }}` with a plain `atm send {{ cc | string | cdata_escape }} --stdin`.{% endif %}]]></step>
  </workflow>
</atm-review>
